28951,cor_28951_3_1.pdf,6,10353," Tender Ref. 01/HR/Noida/Cont/C-3743/9900308536 Name of work /job “Empanelment of Film Producers”. Corrigendum-3 to GePNIC tender ref. no. NTPC/EOC/9900308536 and tender ID no. 2025_NTPC_99429_1 dtd. 18/08/2025 SN Quer y R e ply 1 Please consider Corporate films/Documentaries/ Tv Serials/tvc also in eligibility criteria for the selection in the new empanelment. QR criteria 7.3 as NIT No. 9900308536 and tender ID no. 2025_NTPC_99429_1 dtd. 18/08/2025 stands unaltered and evaluation of bids will be done as per QR. However, industrial/corporate film is defined below: - Industrial/Corporate Film i s a form of audio-visual communication tool which use s facts/data related to the organization as available in the public domain and creatively presents them through the use of graphics, animation, voice over etc for internal/external stakeholders to drive positive narrative and generate goodwill for the company/organization. This can be long or short video format and may be simple documentary (with voice over) or may use storytelling with the help of artists. Corporate Films are primarily produced by in-house communication teams with the help of external agencies and are meant for non-commerc ial advertisement of the organization/company/corporate. In the context of NTPC, we have been utilising Corporate Film for our branding/publicity activity wherein inputs regarding our core business along with other initiatives are comprehensively captured to amplify positive narrative around NTPC ",data/processed/extracted_items/ntpc_text/28951_cor_28951_3_1.txt,
