28985,NIT_Download.pdf,3,7036,"NTPC LTD CORPORATE OPERATION SERVICES, EOC, NOIDA VENDOR ENLISTMENT FOR O&M WORKS PACKAGE ON PAN NTPC BASIS 1 CEG No. MGR-03 2 Brief description of CEG Ultrasonic Flaw Detector (USFD)Testing of MGR rail track & welded Joints in MGR 3 Responsibility Centre ERHQ-I 4 Indicative brief scope of work A-1: RAILS/TRACK ULTRASONIC TESTING (Unit – RMT of Track) Testing of 52 KG Rail ‘or’ 60 KG Rail track by USFD machine for detecting flaw by using probe 0 degree, 30 degree and 70 degree probes or “suitable prob e as per prevailing railway norms” including cleaning of Rail surface by wire brush , providing USFD machine and suitable Battery for this work as per RDSO/M&C/401/2008 or Equivalent or Advanced. All type of probes, all type of tools and tackles and supply of all operators / Labours / supervisors, All consumable & safety items like paints & personal protective Equipment etc. including cleaning the rail surface by wire brush & coolant (water) etc. After completion of Testing: Periodical Test Reports indicating all types of defects in specified Format to be submitted immediately for Rectification. The Agency has to arrange all Safety arrangements towards his USFD Testing Machine and Testing Team Members as well as MGR Track so that Safe Movement of Rolling St ock do not hamper at the time of USFD TESTING. All transportation and protection of USFD testing Machine and Testing Team Members will be in scope of Agency. After identifying any defects i.e. IMR , IMRW, OBS , OBSW, DFW etc,",data/processed/extracted_items/ntpc_text/28985_NIT_Download.txt,
28986,NIT_Download.pdf,2,2457,"NTPC LTD Vendor Enlistment for IT-FMS ( Facility Management Services) on PAN NTPC basis 1 CEG No. IT-01 2 Brief description of CEG IT-FMS (Facility Management Services) Services at NTPC Plant/Location 3 Responsibility Centre VDC 4 Brief scope of work The FMS (Facility Management Services) for to provide the support & services for installed IT -Infrastructures across the plant/stations to ensure the various IT services (Internet. Intranet, Telephone Line Maintenance, AV system, VC System, etc) to take care business needs. 5 Technical Qualifying requirements 1. The Bidder should have its own Establishment/Support Office/Repair/ Service Centre in India. (Relevant document having information about address must be provided) 2. The bidder should have executed the work of "" IT Maintenance Contract/ IT-Support Services/IT Facility Management Services/ Miscellaneous IT infrastructure facility / Maintenance or Support services of Data Networks / Wi-Fi Network/ LAN/WAN. Document to be submitted by Applicant in support of meeting QR 1) Relevant PO copy and Client’s Completion Certificate/RA bill/Final Deviation Statement. 6 Documents to be submitted In addition to the documents required in support of meeting technical requirements as stated above, following documents are required to be submitted by the Applicants applying for enlistment:- 1. Three POs with BOQ of the highest executed values of similar work during previous five years from the date of application and Copy of Completion Cer",data/processed/extracted_items/ntpc_text/28986_NIT_Download.txt,
28987,NIT_Download.pdf,12,23283,"NTPC LTD VEC, RAIPUR Subject: Qualifying requirement for Vendor Enlistment for Supply and Installation of Fills in Cooling Tower(s) A CEG No. OFF-10 A(Cat-I, 50 Lakh to 4.0 Cr) Brief descr iption of MEG Supply and installation of Fills in Cooling Tower(s) Responsibil ity Centre VEC Brief sco pe of work Supply and Installation of new fills and disposal/buyback of old Fills. Note: The detail scope of work & other Terms & conditions would be specified separately in the Tender against the specific requirements ENLISTME NT PROCESS 1) Sub ject enlistment is for enlistment of vendors for “Supply and installat ion of Cooling Tower fills” (Refer Annexure-I for scope of work). 2) Applicants who meet QR criteria at Sl. No. B shall only be enlisted. 3) Enlisted vendors as per their execut ion capability (EC) will be issued tender enquiries for station specific packages. The scope of work of these tenders will generally comprise as detailed in Annexure-I (scope of work) under the station specific tender(s). (Refer Annexure-I for scope of work). B TECHNICAL CRITERIA OF QUALIFYING REQUIREMENT(QR): 1. The applicant should be a manufacturer of ‘Poly Vinyl Chloride (PVC) or Poly Propylene (PP)’ fills for industrial Cooling Tower(s). 2. The applicant should have executed work of Supply and Installation of ‘Fills’ in Cooling Tower(s) having minimum executed value Rs 50 lakhs (Fifty lakhs) , in any single order during last five years as on the last date of submission of the application for enlist",data/processed/extracted_items/ntpc_text/28987_NIT_Download.txt,
28988,NIT_Download.pdf,4,6103,"Subject: Qualifying Requirement (QR) for Vendor Enlistment for Eddy current testing of Condenser & Heat Exchanger tubes in turbine area. (CATEGORY-I Enlistment) NTPC LTD VENDOR ENLISTMENT FOR O&M WORKS PACKAGE ON PAN NTPC BASIS 1 CEG No. TMD-24 2 Brief description of CEG Vendor Enlistment for Eddy current testing of Condenser & Heat Exchanger tubes in turbine area. (CATEGORY-I Enlistment) 3 Responsibility Centre USSC-VEC 4 TECHNICAL Qualifying Requirement The applicant should have executed the work (s) of Eddy Current Testing of Condenser tubes in turbine area of at least one number of steam Turbine with Minimum Unit Size of 200 MW within preceding 05 (ﬁve) years reckoned as on the Last date of submission of application. 5 Brief scope of work 1. The main objective of Eddy Current Testing (ECT) on heat exchanger and condenser tubes is to detect and evaluate surface and subsurface flaws such as corrosion, pitting, wall thinning, cracking, erosion, and tube denting. 2. Agency shall mobilize necessary and qualified manpower (Technicians should be Level II certified in ECT) and Eddy current testing Equipment & accessories, T&P, Consumables & probes, Calibration tube (As per ASTM standard), required for the mentioned job. 3. The agency shall submit test certificate of Eddy current testing machine, and all tools and tackles used in the work. 4. Agency shall make its own arrangement for shifting of materials, T&P etc. required for the completion of work. 5. The Agency shall submit th",data/processed/extracted_items/ntpc_text/28988_NIT_Download.txt,
28989,NIT_Download.pdf,4,6403,"NTPC LTD USSC, VDC-RAIPUR VENDOR ENLISTMENT FOR O&M WORKS PACKAGE ON PAN NTPC BASIS 1 CEG No. TMD-25 2 Brief description of CEG Chemical cleaning of Condenser tubes & Heat Exchanger tubes in turbine area. 3 Responsibility Centre USSC-VEC 4 Brief scope of work 1. Design & Documentation: Complete design and procedure submission for chemical cleaning and neutralization, including schematic diagrams, technical details for NTPC approval. 2. Temporary Setup: Installation of a temporary system including chemical mixing tank, sufficient no. of pumps and drain pipeline to neutralization pit (details shall be provided in the individual tenders). 3. All valves, pipelines, instruments, tools, motors, and scaffolding needed for the setup to be arranged by the agency. 4. Chemical Supply: Supply and testing of cleaning chemicals and corrosion inhibitor shall be in Agency scope or as mentioned in the tender documents. 5. Cleaning Work: Manual/brush cleaning, opening of manholes, fixing dummies, and chemical cleaning through acid circulation per NTPC’s detailed procedure. 6. Cleaning Procedure: Includes water filling, leak testing, acid dosing, temperature control, circulation, pH and parameter monitoring, neutralization, and sludge disposal. 7. Post-cleaning Tasks: High pressure water jet cleaning, scale/foreign material removal, passivation, system flushing, and condenser inspection. 8. Utilities & Support: Agency to arrange heating system; NTPC may supply auxiliary steam. Agency to provide",data/processed/extracted_items/ntpc_text/28989_NIT_Download.txt,
