29419,NIT_Download.pdf,2,3881," NTPC LTD CORPORATE OPERATION SERVICES, EOC, NOIDA VENDOR ENLISTMENT FOR O&M WORKS PACKAGE ON PAN NTPC BASIS 1 CEG No. TMD-18 2 Brief description of CEG Helium leak test for Condenser 3 Responsibility Centre CPC 4 Brief scope of work A. Finding air ingress points in to condenser negative pressure parts for high Dissolved Oxygen (DO) & low vacuum problem by on line Helium leak detection tests in Units of NTPC, categorizing ingresses into very small, small, medium, large and very large with appropriat e tagging at ingress points for easy identification and photographing(digital) of the ingress points. B. Mobilization of Helium leak detector equipment along with accessories, Helium gas (min 03 no’s filled cylinders) and required special tools & tackles and manpower C. Helium leak detector equipment and accessories and tools & tackles and any other consumables required are to be brought by the agency and transportation of the same including transit and other insurances are in the scope of the agency. D. Necessary scaffoldings & platforms required and power supply and lighting arrangements for carrying out the checking works will be provided by NTPC free of charges. 5 Technical Qualifying Requirements The applicant must have successfully carried out Helium leak testing of at least five condensers of 200MW & above capacity units during the preceding five years from the last date of submission of application for enlistment. Document to be submitted by Vendor in support of meeting QR",data/processed/extracted_items/ntpc_text/29419_NIT_Download.txt,
29420,NIT_Download.pdf,4,6103,"Subject: Qualifying Requirement (QR) for Vendor Enlistment for Eddy current testing of Condenser & Heat Exchanger tubes in turbine area. (CATEGORY-I Enlistment) NTPC LTD VENDOR ENLISTMENT FOR O&M WORKS PACKAGE ON PAN NTPC BASIS 1 CEG No. TMD-24 2 Brief description of CEG Vendor Enlistment for Eddy current testing of Condenser & Heat Exchanger tubes in turbine area. (CATEGORY-I Enlistment) 3 Responsibility Centre USSC-VEC 4 TECHNICAL Qualifying Requirement The applicant should have executed the work (s) of Eddy Current Testing of Condenser tubes in turbine area of at least one number of steam Turbine with Minimum Unit Size of 200 MW within preceding 05 (ﬁve) years reckoned as on the Last date of submission of application. 5 Brief scope of work 1. The main objective of Eddy Current Testing (ECT) on heat exchanger and condenser tubes is to detect and evaluate surface and subsurface flaws such as corrosion, pitting, wall thinning, cracking, erosion, and tube denting. 2. Agency shall mobilize necessary and qualified manpower (Technicians should be Level II certified in ECT) and Eddy current testing Equipment & accessories, T&P, Consumables & probes, Calibration tube (As per ASTM standard), required for the mentioned job. 3. The agency shall submit test certificate of Eddy current testing machine, and all tools and tackles used in the work. 4. Agency shall make its own arrangement for shifting of materials, T&P etc. required for the completion of work. 5. The Agency shall submit th",data/processed/extracted_items/ntpc_text/29420_NIT_Download.txt,
29421,NIT_Download.pdf,7,10570," NTPC LTD USSC, VDC-RAIPUR VENDOR ENLISTMENT FOR O&M WORKS PACKAGE ON PAN NTPC BASIS 1 CEG No. TMD-23 2 CEG DESCRIPTION Residual life assessment (RLA) study of steam turbine of 200 MW Units & Above 3 RESPONSIBILITY CENTRE CPG1 / VEC 4 AREA OF EXECUTION OF WORK 1) HP Turbine Rotor and IP Turbine Rotor 2) HP & IP Turbine Casing, Stationary Blades of Turbine, 3) HP/IP Stop & Control Valves. 4) LP Rotor and Casing. 5) High Temperature Bolts & Studs. 6) HP/IP Stop Valves, HP/IP Control Valves 7) High Temperature Bends of Steam Admission Pipe. Different components of Casings, Rotors, Turbine blades, Bearings, Guide blades, Turbine valves, extraction pipes, HP/LP bypass valves & other components are required to be comprehensively evaluated for remaining life of Steam Turbine. 5 BRIEF SCOPE OF WORK for CONTRACTOR HP Turbine Rotor and IP Turbine Rotor: The HP and IP rotor surfaces shall be cleaned and following examination shall be carried out on the rotors. a) Visual examination for thermal cracks on the surface of the rotors. b) Magnetic particle examination and dye penetration test for the complete rotor to be carried out. c) Visual and dimensional examination of blades with shrouds is to be carried out and DP test is to be performed. d) Checking of rotor grooves and sealing visually and MPI for cracks in high temperature zone. All blades of HP/IP rotors to be checked for absence of crack by fluorescent particle inspection (FPI). e) Eddy current / Ultrasonic test on disc near the r",data/processed/extracted_items/ntpc_text/29421_NIT_Download.txt,
29422,NIT_Download.pdf,4,6403,"NTPC LTD USSC, VDC-RAIPUR VENDOR ENLISTMENT FOR O&M WORKS PACKAGE ON PAN NTPC BASIS 1 CEG No. TMD-25 2 Brief description of CEG Chemical cleaning of Condenser tubes & Heat Exchanger tubes in turbine area. 3 Responsibility Centre USSC-VEC 4 Brief scope of work 1. Design & Documentation: Complete design and procedure submission for chemical cleaning and neutralization, including schematic diagrams, technical details for NTPC approval. 2. Temporary Setup: Installation of a temporary system including chemical mixing tank, sufficient no. of pumps and drain pipeline to neutralization pit (details shall be provided in the individual tenders). 3. All valves, pipelines, instruments, tools, motors, and scaffolding needed for the setup to be arranged by the agency. 4. Chemical Supply: Supply and testing of cleaning chemicals and corrosion inhibitor shall be in Agency scope or as mentioned in the tender documents. 5. Cleaning Work: Manual/brush cleaning, opening of manholes, fixing dummies, and chemical cleaning through acid circulation per NTPC’s detailed procedure. 6. Cleaning Procedure: Includes water filling, leak testing, acid dosing, temperature control, circulation, pH and parameter monitoring, neutralization, and sludge disposal. 7. Post-cleaning Tasks: High pressure water jet cleaning, scale/foreign material removal, passivation, system flushing, and condenser inspection. 8. Utilities & Support: Agency to arrange heating system; NTPC may supply auxiliary steam. Agency to provide",data/processed/extracted_items/ntpc_text/29422_NIT_Download.txt,
29423,NIT_Download.pdf,3,5006,"Subject: Qualifying Requirement (QR) for Vendor Enlistment for Online leak sealing in Turbine, Boiler & other areas of power plant. (CATEGORY-I Enlistment) NTPC LTD VENDOR ENLISTMENT FOR O&M WORKS PACKAGE ON PAN NTPC BASIS 1 CEG No. TMD-26 2 Brief description of CEG Vendor Enlistment for Online leak sealing in Turbine, Boiler & other areas of power plant. (CATEGORY-I Enlistment) 3 Responsibility Centre USSC-VEC 4 Area of execution of work Valve / bonnet / Flange / Gland / Pipeline & other area of TG Power Cycle 5 TECHNICAL Qualifying Requirement 1.0 Qualifying Requirements: The applicant who wishes to participate in the bidding shall meet the Qualifying Requirements stipulated hereunder: 1.1 Technical Criteria: The applicant should have executed the work (s) of Online leak sealing work including supply & installation of clamps, in Power plant having minimum 200 MW units , within the preceding 05 (ﬁve) years reckoned as on the Last Date of submission of application. 6 Brief scope of work 1.Work envisaged is attending jobs by on-line leak sealing technique in Valves/pipelines/flanges in Turbine, boiler &other areas. The following types of leakages are to be attended by online sealing method having pressure up to 300Kg/sq cm & temperature up to 600 Deg C. a) Various valves gland leakages. b) Various flange joint leakages and valve bonnet leakages. c) Attending various pipeline leakages. d) Installation & supply of ring /box clamps to attend leakages of valves, flange or pipeline",data/processed/extracted_items/ntpc_text/29423_NIT_Download.txt,
