29702,NIT_Download.pdf,4,6103,"Subject: Qualifying Requirement (QR) for Vendor Enlistment for Eddy current testing of Condenser & Heat Exchanger tubes in turbine area. (CATEGORY-I Enlistment) NTPC LTD VENDOR ENLISTMENT FOR O&M WORKS PACKAGE ON PAN NTPC BASIS 1 CEG No. TMD-24 2 Brief description of CEG Vendor Enlistment for Eddy current testing of Condenser & Heat Exchanger tubes in turbine area. (CATEGORY-I Enlistment) 3 Responsibility Centre USSC-VEC 4 TECHNICAL Qualifying Requirement The applicant should have executed the work (s) of Eddy Current Testing of Condenser tubes in turbine area of at least one number of steam Turbine with Minimum Unit Size of 200 MW within preceding 05 (ﬁve) years reckoned as on the Last date of submission of application. 5 Brief scope of work 1. The main objective of Eddy Current Testing (ECT) on heat exchanger and condenser tubes is to detect and evaluate surface and subsurface flaws such as corrosion, pitting, wall thinning, cracking, erosion, and tube denting. 2. Agency shall mobilize necessary and qualified manpower (Technicians should be Level II certified in ECT) and Eddy current testing Equipment & accessories, T&P, Consumables & probes, Calibration tube (As per ASTM standard), required for the mentioned job. 3. The agency shall submit test certificate of Eddy current testing machine, and all tools and tackles used in the work. 4. Agency shall make its own arrangement for shifting of materials, T&P etc. required for the completion of work. 5. The Agency shall submit th",data/processed/extracted_items/ntpc_text/29702_NIT_Download.txt,
29703,NIT_Download.pdf,3,5006,"Subject: Qualifying Requirement (QR) for Vendor Enlistment for Online leak sealing in Turbine, Boiler & other areas of power plant. (CATEGORY-I Enlistment) NTPC LTD VENDOR ENLISTMENT FOR O&M WORKS PACKAGE ON PAN NTPC BASIS 1 CEG No. TMD-26 2 Brief description of CEG Vendor Enlistment for Online leak sealing in Turbine, Boiler & other areas of power plant. (CATEGORY-I Enlistment) 3 Responsibility Centre USSC-VEC 4 Area of execution of work Valve / bonnet / Flange / Gland / Pipeline & other area of TG Power Cycle 5 TECHNICAL Qualifying Requirement 1.0 Qualifying Requirements: The applicant who wishes to participate in the bidding shall meet the Qualifying Requirements stipulated hereunder: 1.1 Technical Criteria: The applicant should have executed the work (s) of Online leak sealing work including supply & installation of clamps, in Power plant having minimum 200 MW units , within the preceding 05 (ﬁve) years reckoned as on the Last Date of submission of application. 6 Brief scope of work 1.Work envisaged is attending jobs by on-line leak sealing technique in Valves/pipelines/flanges in Turbine, boiler &other areas. The following types of leakages are to be attended by online sealing method having pressure up to 300Kg/sq cm & temperature up to 600 Deg C. a) Various valves gland leakages. b) Various flange joint leakages and valve bonnet leakages. c) Attending various pipeline leakages. d) Installation & supply of ring /box clamps to attend leakages of valves, flange or pipeline",data/processed/extracted_items/ntpc_text/29703_NIT_Download.txt,
